    recent tier: transport: 4 newest sources stay dense
    recent tier: (2,1) slice: unchanged from the shipped chain
    recent tier: elementwise: (3,) slice and Wick scales
    shared tier: transport of Q: P1: one (n,n)@(n,r) serves every age
    shared tier: reconstruction: P2: the Hadamard destroys the rank structure, so every old source must be materialised
    shared tier: (2,1) into r-coords: P2: (n,n)@(n,r) instead of (n,n)@(n,n)
    shared tier: one trailing @ Q^T: the sum is taken in r-coords first
    shared tier: elementwise: (3,) slice and Wick, per source
    basis join (incremental): project-off + thin QR + an (r+c) core eigendecomposition + one rotation. The core step has NO flopscope primitive: priced as arithmetic, and a deployable version must be priced again
    rebase right factors after join: R @ F_s for every source, every join -- the price of sharing, and the family most often forgotten

